# toke — outstanding work register

Everything deliberately deferred, left incomplete against a plan acceptance
criterion, or claimed-but-unverified during Phases 0–3.

Maintained alongside [IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md](IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md). The plan
says what the phases are; this file says what they did not deliver. Add an
entry the moment something is skipped — a deferral that lives only in a commit
message is a deferral nobody will find.

Status: `OPEN` · `BLOCKED` (needs another task first) · `DONE`

Last audited: 2026-09-21, after Phase 6.

---

## 1. Defects — introduced, not deferred

### DEF-1 · Grouped objects disappear from the canvas · DONE · 2026-09-21
`groupSelection` moves children into the group node, so they leave the
top-level array. `StudioCanvas.buildFabricObject` returns `null` for
`kind: 'group'`, and the render loop only walks top-level nodes — so the
children are never drawn.

The P3 e2e asserted the layers **tree** showed three items after grouping and
never checked the canvas, which is exactly how this got through.

**Fixed:** `renderableNodes` flattens groups to leaves in paint order — groups
hold absolute coordinates, so no transform stack is needed. Selecting a group
now selects every leaf inside it.

The viewport exposes `data-fabric-objects`, so browser tests can assert what
Fabric actually holds rather than what the tree claims. Two regression tests
cover place/undo and group/ungroup.

### DEF-2 · Canvas text edits may not reach the store · OPEN · medium
Double-clicking an `IText` enters Fabric's editor. `commitFromFabric` reads
`object.text` on `object:modified`, but Fabric emits `text:changed` and
`editing:exited` for text edits and it is unverified that `object:modified`
fires at all.

- **Accept:** double-click a text object, type, click away; the new string
  survives an undo/redo round trip and appears in the layers tree.

